      ['The President gives assent to it', 'It is published in a newspaper', 'The Supreme Court approves it', 'The Chief Justice signs it'],
      'After a bill is passed by both Houses, it is sent to the President. Only when the President gives assent (Article 111) does the bill become an Act. The courts have no role in approving bills; they may later examine whether an Act is constitutional if someone challenges it.',
