      'A minor\'s agreement is void from the beginning (Mohori Bibee v. Dharmodas Ghose). The rule of estoppel does not apply against a minor, so even a false statement of age does not make him liable. The court may, on equitable grounds, ask him to restore property or money still traceable in his hands.',
